// What can go wrong in this package, and nothing else.
// Running out of memory is not one of those things: a string or a builder that cannot get its storage terminates
// the program, and `TryReserve` and `TryClone` throw the allocator's own `AllocError` for code that can recover.
// What is left says nothing about the machine and everything about where the bytes came from: they are not UTF-8, or
// an offset would cut a character in half.

/// What went wrong.
/// Every case is a failure. An operation that can fail returns its result, or nothing, and declares
/// `throws TextError`, so success is the return value rather than a case here.
/// @see https://rux-lang.dev/docs/api/text/text-error
pub enum TextError: int32 {
    /// The bytes are not well-formed UTF-8.
    InvalidUtf8 = 3,
    /// A byte offset that is not where a character starts, and so not a place text may be cut.
    NotABoundary = 4
}
